Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: fit standard MTU frames behind compact NSS TLVs

The small-memory profile budgets 1816 bytes for a 256-byte descriptor,
but IPQ5018 and QCN6122 retain a 384-byte packet offset in both the HTT
ring filter and NSS SOC_INIT. Only 1432 bytes are left, so normal MTU
traffic consumes two receive buffers and REO descriptors per packet.

Use the firmware-supported 2048-byte buffer size already used by the
larger profile. Keep the hardware TLV offsets, ring depths and pool counts
unchanged. Both HTT and SOC_INIT share this value. On the target AArch64
profile the NSS EMPTY/reusable buffer DMA region covers at least 2048
bytes (1984-byte minimum plus 64-byte NET_SKB_PAD).

Apply after the 256M ring-depth patch, which retains the old budget comment
as context; this changes buffer bytes while preserving that ring sizing.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.h
@@ -30,7 +30,8 @@
-/* 256b desc TLV + 4b(rounded) Pad + 30byte max nwifi header +
- * 18byte mesh hdr + 8byte snap + 1500 eth payload
+/* Buffer bytes, not ring entries. A 384-byte descriptor plus padding,
+ * native Wi-Fi/mesh/SNAP headers and a standard MTU frame must fit.
+ * HTT and NSS SOC_INIT use the same firmware-supported 2K buffer.
  */
-#define ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_NSS_REFILL_RING_SIZE	1816
+#define ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_NSS_REFILL_RING_SIZE	2048
 #else
 /* Num VDEVS per radio */
 #define TARGET_NUM_VDEVS(ab)	(ab->hw_params.num_vdevs_peers[ab->qmi.target_mem_mode].num_vdevs)
